        <item>
            <title>1.0.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 10:14:23 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.0.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[First stable release. Heads Up puts a full-screen alert on every display right before your meetings start, so you actually see it — pulls from your calendars, finds the Zoom/Meet/Teams link automatically, and lets you snooze or join straight from the alert.

What's new since 0.5.3:
- Launch at login, offered on first run and adjustable anytime in Settings
- Update notifications now show real release notes instead of a bare changelog link

Recent fixes:
- Snoozing an alert no longer reopens it within seconds — it now actually waits out the snooze duration you picked
- Join links wrapped by Microsoft Defender Safe Links (common on Microsoft 365) now resolve to the real Zoom/Meet/Teams URL instead of falling back to the wrong link
- Fixed Calendar access never prompting on notarized builds
- Real copyright notice in the About panel
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/rufushonour/headsup/releases/download/v1.0.0/HeadsUp-1.0.0.dmg" length="1890960" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="l+EQm9kuT/ZdRUp75mYGh3KH/9iwDilYyTOtNzNAbg90RRT1krI3jUqW0Qa1roQUBUaPhYb2MPPQFrqZT79MDg=="/>
